# Implementation Plan: Comprehensive Score Tab & MIS Scoring Engine Refinement

Refine and standardize the MIS Score calculations, API endpoints, and user/owner interfaces across all task types (Daily Checklists, Weekly/Monthly Checklists, FMS steps, Delegations, Compliance tasks) and periods (`Daily`, `Weekly`, `Monthly`, `Quarterly`).

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Scoring Invariants & Rules Enforced**:
> 1. **Negative Score Display**: $100\% \text{ completion} \rightarrow \mathbf{0\%}$ (Perfect), $80\% \rightarrow \mathbf{-20\%}$, $0\% \rightarrow \mathbf{-100\%}$. If zero tasks are assigned in a period, both scores display $\mathbf{0\%}$.
> 2. **Task Weights**: Standard tasks = **Weight 1**, Important / Compliance / Delegations = **Weight 3**.
> 3. **4 Periods Supported**: `Daily` (Today IST), `Weekly` (Monday 00:00 to Saturday 23:59 IST), `Monthly` (Current IST Month), `Quarterly` (Current Indian Financial Year Quarter).
> 4. **Late Submission from Score Backlog**: Users can submit past uncompleted tasks from the "Not Done" list, marking them as **Done Late** (Work Done earns credit, On-Time does not).
> 5. **Audit Flags (Flagged FALSE)**: Tasks marked false by the auditor revert to `is_done = false, is_on_time = false` and appear highlighted in pink with auditor details.

